1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,950
Cinderella

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:10,950
Cinderella's sister

3
00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:19,470
Cinderella's Sister

4
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,120
Episode 10

5
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:30,310
No, we'll leave it there for one more day.

6
00:00:30,310 --> 00:00:35,180
It'll only take us a day to bring it back and leaving it there another day won't spoil the wine.

7
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:38,160
I'll find a different method by tomorrow.

8
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:44,140
Just leave the container, don't touch it and go.

9
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:46,460
I'll be hanging up.

10
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:20,210
What are you doing in this office?

11
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:24,320
Jeong Woo, please call Hyo Seon for me.

12
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:27,230
There is something I have to ask Hyo Seon.

13
00:01:27,230 --> 00:01:32,690
Those clients at the Japanese hotel...

14
00:01:32,690 --> 00:01:35,210
You know, the one with the son, who invited Hyo Seon home because her son liked her.

15
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:40,680
I'd like to find out if she still keeps in touch with her.

16
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:45,770
No, there's no need to ask.

17
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:49,850
Get yourself together.

18
00:01:49,850 --> 00:01:52,970
You shouldn't be doing this here. Let's go.

19
00:01:55,210 --> 00:01:57,950
Condolences

20
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:35,950
How come you and I already have to greet each other like this?

21
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:44,330
I have nothing to say to you.

22
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:47,500
Aigoo, Brother-in-law.

23
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:52,490
How do I live?

24
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:56,480
How do I live without Joon Soo's dad?

25
00:03:03,090 --> 00:03:06,090
Aigoo, poor man.

26
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:09,760
What is this bolt from the blue?

27
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:13,310
Aigoo, you poor thing!

28
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:16,260
What did I tell you long ago?

29
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:21,130
I said you need to be careful about who you welcome into your family!

30
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:23,890
Aigoo, Honey!

31
00:03:23,890 --> 00:03:26,700
Your aunt has come!

32
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:30,670
The aunt that you loved so much has come!

33
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:34,600
What are you doing wherever you are?

34
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:44,320
How could you die and go at such a young age?

35
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:49,790
Aigoo, Joon Soo's father!

36
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:53,590
Aigoo, Joon Soo loved you so much!

37
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:57,320
What are you doing wherever you are?!

38
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:24,150
Hyo Seon.

39
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,260
Oppa.

40
00:04:30,150 --> 00:04:34,270
I'm really in big trouble.

41
00:04:34,270 --> 00:04:37,160
No matter how much I drink,

42
00:04:38,060 --> 00:04:40,380
I don't get drunk.

43
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:54,890
No matter how much I try, I can't believe it.

44
00:04:54,890 --> 00:04:57,840
I wanted to see if I could bring myself to believe it if I got drunk,

45
00:04:57,840 --> 00:05:01,350
So, I ended up drinking two whole jars.

46
00:05:04,410 --> 00:05:07,840
But, I still can't believe it at all.

47
00:05:14,310 --> 00:05:16,060
Hyo Seon.

48
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:18,380
Don't do it.

49
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,700
Don't do it!

50
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:23,510
- Hyo Seon.
- I said don't do that!

51
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:29,230
You won't even let me rely on you,

52
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:32,200
Why are you even taking away my alcohol.

53
00:05:33,930 --> 00:05:35,830
Oppa...

54
00:05:37,620 --> 00:05:39,430
Get lost.

55
00:05:42,490 --> 00:05:44,600
I said to get lost!

56
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:50,280
You get lost,

57
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:53,690
and take Eun Jo too.

58
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:04,060
The export order... I was against it.

59
00:06:06,650 --> 00:06:09,320
But, Eun Jo insisted.

60
00:06:10,810 --> 00:06:15,820
If it weren't for Eun Jo, Dad wouldn't have done it.

61
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:21,560
No matter whatever Eun Jo said, Dad always...

62
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:26,250
No matter how many spiteful words Eun Joo said,

63
00:06:27,870 --> 00:06:31,150
Dad trusted her like a fool.

64
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:37,710
If it weren''t for Eun Joo, dad wouldn't have become like this.

65
00:06:39,150 --> 00:06:41,720
It wasn't Eun Joo, but

66
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:43,910
it was me.

67
00:06:43,910 --> 00:06:46,390
I did that.

68
00:06:53,550 --> 00:06:55,940
That evil bitch.

69
00:06:57,900 --> 00:07:00,620
I'll kill her.

70
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:04,220
I won't let her get away with this.

71
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:18,660
Let's send Ahjussi off properly.

72
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,740
Right now,

73
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:29,460
let's just think about sending him off well.

74
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:31,150
Hyo Seon.

75
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:36,900
He can't go like this, Oppa.

76
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:46,480
To where... And how can I send Dad off?

77
00:07:53,110 --> 00:07:59,260
I can't even believe that I'm wearing these kinds of clothes right now.

78
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:06,310
So how are you telling me to send Dad off when I don't know where he's going, Oppa?!

79
00:08:46,210 --> 00:08:47,850
Noona.

80
00:08:47,850 --> 00:08:49,950
I have a lot to do.

81
00:08:49,950 --> 00:08:52,480
I have to go to the factory,

82
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:55,350
and I don't know when the last time I went to the research lab was.

83
00:08:55,350 --> 00:08:57,220
Get ahold of yourself.

84
00:08:57,770 --> 00:08:59,670
Let me go.

85
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:02,190
I have to go to the factory.

86
00:09:02,190 --> 00:09:04,500
Get ahold of yourself!

87
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:07,460
You need to come to your senses and do what needs to be done.

88
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:11,620
Greet the guests and negotiate burial preparations with the elders.

89
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:14,170
There are too many things you have to do.

90
00:09:14,170 --> 00:09:16,150
Ahjumma only cries.

91
00:09:16,150 --> 00:09:19,380
Joon Soo's little noona has disappeared and I don't know where she is...

92
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:21,660
No one's in their right mind now.

93
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:24,130
Noona.

94
00:09:24,130 --> 00:09:29,960
Dae Seong True Wine Makers and President Goo Dae Seong's funeral are all a mess.

95
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,990
Are you going to leave it like that?

96
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:44,250
The funeral of President Goo Dae Seong of Dae Seong True Wine Makers

97
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:45,860
That's right.

98
00:09:51,230 --> 00:10:02,020
The funeral of President Goo Dae Seong of Dae Seong True Wine Makers.

99
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,610
Yes.

100
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:14,700
Condolences

101
00:10:17,430 --> 00:10:21,130
You're coming to your senses now, right?

102
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:12,960
He's waiting for you...

103
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:19,870
If it's a relationship like ours, one phone call (In Japanese)

104
00:11:19,870 --> 00:11:24,440
is enough to be the same as signing a contract.

105
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:27,720
But still, let's formally put this on a document and each get one copy.

106
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,820
It'll be like a contract,

107
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:33,040
but won't it's contents be more like

108
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:36,250
our companies sending love letters?

109
00:11:37,490 --> 00:11:40,570
Your skills are really good, Hyung.

110
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:42,010
Hyung Gi Jeong.

111
00:11:42,010 --> 00:11:47,130
Miss Miura, something suddenly came up.

112
00:11:47,130 --> 00:11:51,770
I'll take care of it and call you back.

113
00:11:54,650 --> 00:11:59,140
You're here? It's a bit earlier than our scheduled time.

114
00:12:01,330 --> 00:12:03,230
Have a seat.

115
00:12:03,230 --> 00:12:07,270
I ... didn't intend that.

116
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,920
Though I'm sure you won't believe me.

117
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:15,280
My goal was to make sure you didn't get Dae Seong True Winemakers.

118
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:18,880
I had no intentions of taking over Dae Seong True Winemakers.

119
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:23,070
After taking it instead of you,

120
00:12:25,410 --> 00:12:27,570
I was going to return it to them.

121
00:12:27,570 --> 00:12:29,500
Because of me,

122
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:33,130
do you know what happened?

123
00:12:33,130 --> 00:12:36,090
Do you know what you've done to me?

124
00:12:39,610 --> 00:12:44,770
I brought you came here just to talk business peacefully..

125
00:12:44,770 --> 00:12:46,760
Stop looking at Dae Seong now.

126
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:50,750
Don't do anything! I won't let you do anything.

127
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:54,070
Are you saying that after you've thought of everything you've done?

128
00:12:54,070 --> 00:12:55,510
Sit down.

129
00:12:55,510 --> 00:12:57,690
Why did you do that

130
00:12:59,170 --> 00:13:01,010
to my mom?

131
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:06,230
When my mom came and asked to see me just once,

132
00:13:06,230 --> 00:13:09,720
why did you make my mom who couldn't run, run?

133
00:13:10,830 --> 00:13:12,760
Who said that?

134
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:16,310
Did Father say that?

135
00:13:16,310 --> 00:13:20,910
Why did you do it? Did you need to do that?

136
00:13:21,990 --> 00:13:24,860
I've tried thinking about it from your perspective.

137
00:13:26,110 --> 00:13:30,090
Since your mom hurt because of my mom,

138
00:13:30,090 --> 00:13:32,750
I thought if I were you, I would also dislike my mom.

139
00:13:32,750 --> 00:13:36,320
Since my mom even had me, he must hate my mom.

140
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:40,080
Just like me, I believed that both of you hyungs suffered.

141
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,740
Like that...

142
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:47,290
Did you want to re-chew memories that don't even exist?

143
00:13:47,290 --> 00:13:48,830
Stop it right now.

144
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:52,800
No matter how much you disliked her, how could a person do that to another person?

145
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,770
That isn't something you should've done!

146
00:13:55,770 --> 00:13:58,380
What else could I do? She knew I was hiding you.

147
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:00,780
I ran because I was sick of it.

148
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:03,820
The one who chased me until the end was your mother.

149
00:14:03,820 --> 00:14:05,530
I didn't tell her to run.

150
00:14:05,530 --> 00:14:10,510
You knew it would take a toll on my mom to run, but you didn't stop.

151
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:12,790
Why are you looking at me like that?

152
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:15,550
Are you implying I ran on purpose?

153
00:14:15,550 --> 00:14:19,900
I did, too. Because of you.

154
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:24,450
I wanted to get something first so it wouldn't go to you,

155
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:28,330
and someone died as a consequence.

156
00:14:30,350 --> 00:14:35,490
Just like I can't forgive myself, I can't forgive you.

157
00:14:37,130 --> 00:14:42,080
Now, I really can't go back to before.

158
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,690
It's because of you.

159
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:49,220
I'm so grateful that I'm going crazy.

160
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:54,130
Dae Sung True Winemakers won't die.

161
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:57,690
You must hope that everything gets destroyed as it disintegrates into the air.

162
00:14:57,690 --> 00:15:01,770
I'm sure you want to become the only seller in the rice wine market, without any competitors!

163
00:15:01,770 --> 00:15:04,390
But that won't happen.

164
00:15:04,390 --> 00:15:06,260
Give it up.

165
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:09,750
Don't do anything to Dae Seong True Winemakers.

166
00:15:09,750 --> 00:15:11,560
If you do,

167
00:15:13,130 --> 00:15:15,560
I won't just stay still.

168
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:22,630
If you don't stay still, what will you do?

169
00:15:23,730 --> 00:15:26,020
I'm going to take you

170
00:15:28,290 --> 00:15:30,410
and die together.

171
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:33,580
Mom!!

172
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:38,590
Joon Soo, go outside and play.

173
00:16:38,590 --> 00:16:44,100
Tell the kitchen ahjummas to give you some cinnamon punch, have it before you play.

174
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:59,430
Because I can't visit you one by one, I apologize for making all of you walk this far to gather here instead.

175
00:17:00,170 --> 00:17:04,450
After the funeral, I had a few immediate things to take care of,

176
00:17:04,450 --> 00:17:06,690
so I lacked a lot of time.

177
00:17:06,690 --> 00:17:09,690
Regarding the incident in Japan last time,

178
00:17:09,690 --> 00:17:13,010
thanks to an influential person who had connections with Hyo Seon,

179
00:17:13,010 --> 00:17:17,540
we were able to sell half of the containter's content in our shipment to Japan to the Japanese market.

180
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:22,430
The remaining half of the shipment was brought back and taken care of by Dae Seong True Winemakers.

181
00:17:22,430 --> 00:17:25,110
What you mean, taken care of by Dae Seonng True Winemakers?

182
00:17:25,110 --> 00:17:29,170
In Japan, we took care of the sales as an ingredient for vinegar.

183
00:17:29,170 --> 00:17:31,410
And I drank

184
00:17:32,610 --> 00:17:34,790
the remaining half.

185
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:48,610
If it were as promised, this is a time for me to start repaying you all for the money you've loaned us,

186
00:17:48,610 --> 00:17:53,480
but apologetically, I am unable to do that at this time.

187
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:59,380
However, because Dae Seong True Winemakers has strong roots,

188
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:06,050
I am certain we will be able to regain our reputation from before.

189
00:18:06,050 --> 00:18:09,150
You all trusted this point,

190
00:18:09,150 --> 00:18:14,120
and thus lent us what was to many of you, your entire life's savings.

191
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:16,120
If you please just wait a little more,

192
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:20,990
Hyo Seon and I will work together to repay you as soon as possible.

193
00:18:20,990 --> 00:18:23,920
If we can't wait any longer, what are you going to do?

194
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:27,930
Of course, I would like to wait for you until the end,

195
00:18:27,930 --> 00:18:31,340
if only Dae Seong hadn't such a poor reputation.

196
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:35,270
I could wait for it, whether that be two years or three years.

197
00:18:35,270 --> 00:18:41,520
However, how can I trust you young ones?

198
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:46,040
I heard that you were able to get profits on at least half the exports to Japan.

199
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:49,880
With that, I need to take care of urgent matters.

200
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:52,530
Hey, are you the only ones with urgent issues?

201
00:18:52,530 --> 00:18:55,490
Who here doesn't have urgent circumstances, that you would be the one to claim those?

202
00:18:55,490 --> 00:18:58,690
Of course. You shouldn't be the one to claim that.

203
00:18:58,690 --> 00:19:03,490
Hyung-nim, if you say such things, it upsets me.

204
00:19:03,490 --> 00:19:06,200
How could you say that knowing my circumstances-

205
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,330
Who are you to raise your voice in front of your elders?

206
00:19:08,330 --> 00:19:10,900
What do you mean, raise my voice?

207
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:13,810
- I am only-
- Cut it out!

208
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:18,770
What measures are you going to take?

209
00:19:18,770 --> 00:19:21,560
Don't you have some sort of plan?

210
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:24,560
We will give you shares proportionate

211
00:19:25,810 --> 00:19:29,700
to your loans to Dae Seong True Winemakers.

212
00:19:30,450 --> 00:19:36,220
All of you here will become owners of Dae Seong True Winemakers.

213
00:19:38,310 --> 00:19:43,280
If you all will take responsibility for the success of Dae Seong True Winemakers.

214
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:45,200
our late

215
00:19:52,050 --> 00:19:59,750
our late... President Goo Dae Seong will also be happy.

216
00:20:09,530 --> 00:20:11,550
Small Noona!

217
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:14,530
Small Noona!

218
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:21,080
- What?
- Let's play.

219
00:20:21,610 --> 00:20:23,870
Let's play later.

220
00:20:23,870 --> 00:20:26,550
Let's play right now.

221
00:20:26,550 --> 00:20:29,230
Play with Big Noona.

222
00:20:30,770 --> 00:20:34,210
Big Noona is a person who doesn't play with Joon Soo.

223
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:45,560
Little Noona is a person who plays with Joon Soo a little bit.

224
00:20:46,490 --> 00:20:49,980
Mom won't play with me most of the time.

225
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:54,700
Dad always plays with Joon Soo.

226
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:58,780
Why won't Dad come back?

227
00:20:59,490 --> 00:21:03,450
Huh? Why isn't Dad back?

228
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:45,210
Noona, there are lots of rocks there.

229
00:21:45,210 --> 00:21:48,510
Sure. Can you get one for me too?

230
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:14,760
I'm curious about something.

231
00:22:17,110 --> 00:22:19,200
I thought that you

232
00:22:21,230 --> 00:22:26,280
had actually liked Dad quite a bit.

233
00:22:28,050 --> 00:22:32,590
But you didn't shed a tear,

234
00:22:34,580 --> 00:22:38,260
From the kitchen granny and all the staff,

235
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:41,380
there wasn't a single person who didn't cry.

236
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:46,630
How can you do that?

237
00:22:47,690 --> 00:22:49,900
What is it that you're curious about?

238
00:22:50,940 --> 00:22:59,360
Weren't you being sincere in front of Dad?

239
00:22:59,360 --> 00:23:04,590
Do you think I'll answer that question?

240
00:23:06,010 --> 00:23:07,990
Tell me.

241
00:23:07,990 --> 00:23:12,650
Did you have any sincerity for my dad at all?

242
00:23:13,430 --> 00:23:16,290
Why? What?

243
00:23:16,290 --> 00:23:18,260
What are you looking at?

244
00:23:18,260 --> 00:23:22,420
- What's sincerity?
- What?

245
00:23:22,420 --> 00:23:25,990
What does this thing called sincerity mean exactly?

246
00:23:25,990 --> 00:23:29,290
Is it nothing to you that my dad passed away?

247
00:23:29,290 --> 00:23:32,840
How can you be so stoic? How can this be nothing?

248
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:36,360
If it weren't for you, this wouldn't have happened, Unni!

249
00:23:37,020 --> 00:23:38,810
So what?

250
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:41,570
What?

251
00:23:41,570 --> 00:23:44,860
So what is it you want me to do?

252
00:23:44,860 --> 00:23:49,920
Now that I think about it, it seems like you're saying your dad died because of me.

253
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:53,880
- What should I do?
- What should you do?

254
00:23:55,010 --> 00:23:58,270
If I tell you to do something, can you actually do it?

255
00:23:58,270 --> 00:24:00,730
Can you do anything?

256
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:03,280
Then bring my dad back to life.

257
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:05,110
Bring my dad back to life!

258
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:09,730
Because I miss him to death, bring my dad back to life!

259
00:24:15,140 --> 00:24:17,320
How could this happen?

260
00:24:19,110 --> 00:24:21,350
It's terrible.

261
00:24:22,970 --> 00:24:28,240
It doesn't make sense. It really doesn't make any sense.

262
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:38,980
I'm scared, Unni.

263
00:24:40,730 --> 00:24:43,350
I'm scared to death.

264
00:24:45,340 --> 00:24:51,340
It feels like I'm standing outside not wearing anything.

265
00:24:52,910 --> 00:24:54,930
I'm cold...

266
00:24:56,510 --> 00:24:58,580
and I'm scared.

267
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:03,540
Unni.

268
00:25:25,540 --> 00:25:29,620
Don't cry.

269
00:25:34,330 --> 00:25:38,100
Don't cry.

270
00:25:39,290 --> 00:25:41,720
Don't cry, Hyo Seon.

271
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:48,630
Don't cry, Hyo Seon.

272
00:25:53,320 --> 00:25:55,220
Don't cry.

273
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:29,040
Until when are you going to keep on crying?

274
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:32,740
The elders say they don't need either stocks or shares. They're demanding that we repay their money immediately,

275
00:26:32,740 --> 00:26:34,970
We have to give them money now.

276
00:26:34,970 --> 00:26:38,750
The last of the yeast that your father made is all gone now.

277
00:26:38,750 --> 00:26:41,630
We have to solve this yeast issue by ourselves now.

278
00:26:41,630 --> 00:26:46,090
And I don't have confidence to produce wine that tastes the same way it did when your father made it.

279
00:26:46,090 --> 00:26:48,260
There's still so much to take care of.

280
00:26:48,260 --> 00:26:52,030
Why is it that all you do is cry every day?

281
00:26:55,300 --> 00:26:57,010
Even if it's just once,

282
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:01,330
can't you comfort me?

283
00:27:01,330 --> 00:27:03,800
Noona, rocks!

284
00:27:04,670 --> 00:27:10,480
Even now, since I'm scared and lonely, I want you Unni

285
00:27:12,550 --> 00:27:17,400
to cherish me at least a little,

286
00:27:18,790 --> 00:27:21,910
then I'll feel like I'll be less scared..

287
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:28,140
Okay?

288
00:27:28,140 --> 00:27:30,380
I'm so sick and tired of your whining, you idiot!

289
00:27:30,380 --> 00:27:33,100
Please stop, I'm begging you!

290
00:27:46,060 --> 00:27:49,970
Evil witch! I'm telling Dad...

291
00:28:10,660 --> 00:28:13,110
What are you all doing right now?

292
00:28:14,550 --> 00:28:17,030
Why have you all given up?

293
00:28:17,520 --> 00:28:21,460
It's the middle of a work day, but why is everyone like this?

294
00:28:21,460 --> 00:28:24,660
Is it all right for you to be acting this way now that the President is no longer with us?

295
00:28:25,970 --> 00:28:27,520
What is this?

296
00:28:28,650 --> 00:28:30,450
Aren't you going to work?

297
00:28:30,450 --> 00:28:32,970
Is there anything for us to do now?

298
00:28:32,970 --> 00:28:36,920
- What?
- There is no work for us.

299
00:28:36,920 --> 00:28:40,330
There aren't any orders, what work are we supposed to do?

300
00:28:40,330 --> 00:28:43,790
I'm going to make the yeast. So, please get ready.

301
00:28:43,790 --> 00:28:48,200
- Will you be able to make the yeast?
- What do you mean?

302
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:50,640
And who'll examine the yeast after?

303
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:52,310
Are you saying now that I won't be able to make the yeast

304
00:28:52,310 --> 00:28:55,150
because there's no one to test it?

305
00:28:55,990 --> 00:28:58,480
I'm asking what you're doing!

306
00:28:58,480 --> 00:29:00,740
Why are you all like this, really?!

307
00:29:00,750 --> 00:29:03,200
Even when the factory and winery were both in trouble,

308
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:06,140
we still paid every single penny of your salary.

309
00:29:06,140 --> 00:29:10,240
Are you saying you're not going to work even though you're getting paid as normal?

310
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:13,990
If you don't want to work, then quit immediately!

311
00:29:49,060 --> 00:29:50,870
It's okay.

312
00:30:14,530 --> 00:30:18,270
Do you think the ahjussies won't feel the loss?

313
00:30:18,270 --> 00:30:21,430
Because President has left us, they're feeling low.

314
00:30:21,430 --> 00:30:24,100
There's no need to push them like that.

315
00:30:24,100 --> 00:30:28,690
Learn some things from Hyo Seon. To become kind and cheerful.

316
00:30:28,690 --> 00:30:31,950
Hyo Seon is very good at not hurting other people's feelings.

317
00:30:41,050 --> 00:30:42,760
Take a look at this.

318
00:30:44,290 --> 00:30:47,470
Do you remember the trash-filled dumpling scandal?

319
00:30:47,470 --> 00:30:50,950
Back then, there was a small business unfairly involved,

320
00:30:50,950 --> 00:30:55,550
The company got embroiled and went bankrupt even before the real facts were confirmed.

321
00:30:55,550 --> 00:30:58,970
Later, that company was found to be innocent,

322
00:30:58,970 --> 00:31:02,330
but the articles that spoke of its innocence were only a few.

323
00:31:02,330 --> 00:31:06,120
Let's draw parallels between that incident and our company problem and make a plea to the media.

324
00:31:06,120 --> 00:31:11,320
Write something. Because I'm good at reading, I don't have a talent for writing.

325
00:31:11,320 --> 00:31:13,980
If you write it, I'll review it.

326
00:31:16,660 --> 00:31:18,500
Are you listening?

327
00:31:35,390 --> 00:31:39,650
Starting tomorrow, you should know that we will not be coming to work.

328
00:31:39,650 --> 00:31:42,540
Manager Kim, what do you mean by saying that?

329
00:31:42,540 --> 00:31:46,860
This is the company, and we know we are your subordinates,

330
00:31:46,860 --> 00:31:48,910
but, we're still your elders!

331
00:31:48,910 --> 00:31:51,490
What on earth have you learned from the President?

332
00:31:51,490 --> 00:31:55,560
Once in a while, he yelled at us for not doing things the way he liked.

333
00:31:55,560 --> 00:31:58,280
But he never hurt our dignity.

334
00:31:58,280 --> 00:32:02,180
We can't work here while being treated this way by someone young enough to be our daughter.

335
00:32:02,180 --> 00:32:05,310
You know that now. Let's get going.

336
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:08,990
Manager Kim! Ahjussi!

337
00:32:09,750 --> 00:32:11,620
Ahjussies!

338
00:32:20,170 --> 00:32:21,950
Hyo Seon is here.

339
00:32:21,950 --> 00:32:24,430
Joon Soo is here.

340
00:32:34,970 --> 00:32:37,260
We're back.

341
00:32:39,740 --> 00:32:42,750
Joon Soo, let's go wash our hands.

342
00:32:42,750 --> 00:32:47,160
Where did you take a kid who has a cold?

343
00:32:47,160 --> 00:32:49,130
Do you know how long I was looking for him?

344
00:32:49,130 --> 00:32:52,520
If you were going to take him out, you should have told me.

345
00:32:52,520 --> 00:32:55,540
Okay, Mom.

346
00:32:56,940 --> 00:32:59,690
I just thought you were sleeping.

347
00:32:59,690 --> 00:33:02,690
What on earth are you going to do if Joon Soo's cold gets worse?!

348
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:05,560
Hurry come in!

349
00:33:11,710 --> 00:33:17,070
I'll help him wash up! I also have to wash up anyway!

350
00:33:19,630 --> 00:33:22,450
We're done. It feels good, right?

351
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:26,700
Here we go.

352
00:33:28,350 --> 00:33:30,590
Mom, I'll help him wash up.

353
00:33:30,590 --> 00:33:32,970
Get away!

354
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:37,750
Let's go.

355
00:33:57,590 --> 00:34:01,760
Is this it? This is what you're doing to me?

356
00:34:02,980 --> 00:34:07,340
In the end, you made me a widow again.

357
00:34:09,350 --> 00:34:13,420
You guys are crazy. You're out of your mind.

358
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,910
Did you guys make a bet

359
00:34:15,910 --> 00:34:20,100
on how terrible this woman's fate can get through your hands?

360
00:34:21,570 --> 00:34:23,450
Do you think I'll break down?

361
00:34:23,450 --> 00:34:27,130
I'm Song Kang Sook!

362
00:34:27,130 --> 00:34:30,350
If I break down, I will hang onto you and bring you down with me.

363
00:34:30,350 --> 00:34:32,520
You think I'll go down alone?

364
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:35,350
Don't even think about it.

365
00:34:36,620 --> 00:34:38,560
Mom.

366
00:34:45,660 --> 00:34:47,520
Mom...

367
00:34:51,120 --> 00:34:53,510
Mom, I was wrong.

368
00:34:54,210 --> 00:34:57,550
I didn't know Joon Soo had a cold.

369
00:35:04,070 --> 00:35:05,850
Don't touch me!

370
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:08,780
Just you try clinging onto me!

371
00:35:08,780 --> 00:35:12,810
It disgusts me when you try clinging onto me. Got it?

372
00:35:29,430 --> 00:35:34,660
♫ In the solictude which wakes me up ♫

373
00:35:36,860 --> 00:35:41,920
♫ when I wake up from an exhausted sleep ♫

374
00:35:44,030 --> 00:35:50,670
♫ because I still remember you smiling ♫

375
00:35:50,670 --> 00:35:56,630
♫ I'm secretly smiling ♫

376
00:35:59,020 --> 00:36:04,930
♫ Love leaves again this way ♫

377
00:36:06,370 --> 00:36:11,740
♫ When the beautiful season arrives ♫

378
00:36:13,680 --> 00:36:20,170
♫ In the sadness you left in the longing ♫

379
00:36:20,170 --> 00:36:25,760
♫ I walk this street again ♫

380
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:33,080
♫ I am living day after day  ♫

381
00:36:33,080 --> 00:36:42,120
♫ In your name when tears appear, ah  ♫

382
00:36:42,130 --> 00:36:44,790
♫ I can't bear it  ♫

383
00:36:44,790 --> 00:36:49,600
♫ So I can't laugh ♫

384
00:36:49,600 --> 00:36:57,040
♫ I'll call out your name again ♫

385
00:36:58,020 --> 00:37:04,050
♫ I'm living life recklessly ♫

386
00:37:04,050 --> 00:37:10,420
♫ When I yearn for love again ♫

387
00:37:11,120 --> 00:37:15,450
Read after you finish your food.

388
00:37:15,450 --> 00:37:22,100
I told you to finish eating first.

389
00:37:24,970 --> 00:37:29,260
♫ I am living day after day  ♫

390
00:37:29,260 --> 00:37:32,710
Mom.

391
00:37:33,510 --> 00:37:36,950
Chew well before you swallow, Joon Soo. Don't get sick anymore.

392
00:37:36,950 --> 00:37:39,080
You must not get sick, okay?

393
00:37:39,080 --> 00:37:40,350
Yes.

394
00:37:41,370 --> 00:37:43,890
♫ I can't bear it  ♫

395
00:37:43,890 --> 00:37:47,110
♫ So I can't laugh ♫

396
00:37:47,160 --> 00:37:49,270
Article Submission

397
00:37:49,290 --> 00:37:57,530
♫ I'll call out your name again ♫

398
00:38:00,720 --> 00:38:02,790
Article Submission
Submitted by Goo Eun Jo, Dae Seong True Winemakers

399
00:38:19,370 --> 00:38:21,760
Your words are too fierce.

400
00:38:21,760 --> 00:38:25,820
It's convincing enough if you just calmly lay out the facts.

401
00:38:26,590 --> 00:38:30,230
People will get fed up reading something excessively emotional like this.

402
00:38:30,230 --> 00:38:32,360
Excessive?

403
00:38:32,360 --> 00:38:35,960
- Did you just say excessive?
- Yes.

404
00:38:35,960 --> 00:38:40,050
I'm someone who completely stands on Dae Seong Co.'s side,

405
00:38:40,050 --> 00:38:43,630
but even I got fed up after reading a couple of lines.

406
00:38:43,630 --> 00:38:47,250
No publications would accept this kind of article.

407
00:38:48,080 --> 00:38:50,070
Write it again.

408
00:38:50,070 --> 00:38:52,110
Where are you going?

409
00:38:52,110 --> 00:38:54,880
Explain to me exactly how it's excessive, line by line.

410
00:38:54,880 --> 00:38:57,890
Right now, persuading them is more important than giving you an explanation.

411
00:38:57,890 --> 00:39:00,190
I failed to persuade the ajusshis.

412
00:39:00,190 --> 00:39:04,560
After you've re-written it, go to the ahjussies, kneel down and beg them for their forgiveness while rubbing your hands.

413
00:39:04,560 --> 00:39:06,850
Are you crazy? Why would I beg them?

414
00:39:06,850 --> 00:39:09,440
- I haven't done anything wrong.
- You didn't do anything wrong?

415
00:39:09,440 --> 00:39:14,290
I don't need people who get paid to just play around either. I'll just hire new people.

416
00:39:14,290 --> 00:39:17,050
If it's so easy, then do it.

417
00:39:17,050 --> 00:39:20,340
They're workers who have accumulated experience at Dae Seong Co. for more than 20 years.

418
00:39:20,340 --> 00:39:22,700
If there are people who can replace them, then do it!

419
00:39:22,700 --> 00:39:24,690
Go ahead and try.

420
00:39:37,810 --> 00:39:39,730
I'd like to look at this one.

421
00:40:01,970 --> 00:40:03,890
How could you...?

422
00:40:06,480 --> 00:40:10,870
I wasn't able to offer my condolences. I've come too late.

423
00:40:13,030 --> 00:40:15,770
You can see Dae Seong in every corner.

424
00:40:17,150 --> 00:40:20,630
This winery reflects Dae Seong's character exactly.

425
00:40:21,820 --> 00:40:26,360
Please leave. It's not right for you to be here.

426
00:40:28,080 --> 00:40:31,040
Let me sample some free wine.

427
00:40:39,570 --> 00:40:42,070
Hurry up and just say what you came here to say.

428
00:40:44,230 --> 00:40:46,610
Give me back my money.

429
00:40:50,480 --> 00:40:55,450
Didn't you take my money to buy rice? Give me back that money immediately.

430
00:40:55,450 --> 00:40:57,890
It's not possible now.

431
00:40:58,520 --> 00:41:02,430
- Then, I'll take the winery.
- Father.

432
00:41:02,430 --> 00:41:08,420
Where is that girl that's working on developing the yeast? Can I see her?

433
00:41:09,630 --> 00:41:12,840
I heard that you gave Ji Seong a piece of your mind.

434
00:41:12,890 --> 00:41:16,900
He said you acted as if you were the gatekeeper

435
00:41:16,900 --> 00:41:19,590
to protect Dae Seong True Winemakers from now on.

436
00:41:19,610 --> 00:41:22,100
Is that really true?

437
00:41:22,980 --> 00:41:27,940
What's the point of protecting Dae Seong Co. when it's already done for?

438
00:41:30,490 --> 00:41:35,990
I‘ll pay a little more to what they owe me, so tell them to just give me the winery.

439
00:41:38,470 --> 00:41:44,380
Thinking Dae Seong True Winemakers without Dae Seong means little,

440
00:41:44,390 --> 00:41:47,620
I was just going to give it up,

441
00:41:48,670 --> 00:41:52,410
but as I looked around the factory and winery...

442
00:41:52,410 --> 00:41:54,850
I realized I must have it.

443
00:42:00,990 --> 00:42:03,480
Pay the money back by next month.

444
00:42:04,420 --> 00:42:09,450
You can give me Dae Sung Do Ga instead of money.

445
00:42:27,200 --> 00:42:31,240
It's too much money for us to handle. We won't make it by next month. Please give us more time.

446
00:42:31,240 --> 00:42:33,260
It's also too much for me to handle.

447
00:42:33,260 --> 00:42:38,270
You turned your back on me, so I must get my money back at least.

448
00:42:39,070 --> 00:42:40,750
Father.

449
00:42:43,870 --> 00:42:46,680
You are groveling right now.

450
00:42:46,680 --> 00:42:49,760
It would be best for you to just give up.

451
00:43:00,490 --> 00:43:04,580
I asked the savings bank to see if the repayment period can be extended.

452
00:43:05,440 --> 00:43:07,770
They said it's impossible.

453
00:43:07,770 --> 00:43:11,480
What if we can't pay it back, do we have to hand over the winery?

454
00:43:11,480 --> 00:43:15,620
Yes, since the president used the winery as collateral.

455
00:43:15,620 --> 00:43:20,760
And now, we can't even go to any of our relatives in the family to ask for help.

456
00:43:20,760 --> 00:43:23,030
What are we going to do?

457
00:43:24,300 --> 00:43:26,330
I'll get things arranged somehow.

458
00:43:26,330 --> 00:43:28,310
I'll try to get it somehow.

459
00:43:28,310 --> 00:43:30,280
Why would you?

460
00:43:31,090 --> 00:43:33,220
What does this have to do with you?

461
00:43:36,520 --> 00:43:40,840
Do you have to talk like that?

462
00:43:46,140 --> 00:43:47,610
What?

463
00:43:47,610 --> 00:43:49,890
- Give me the money.
- I don't know what money you want me to give you?!

464
00:43:49,890 --> 00:43:51,830
I'm sure you have the money that ahjussi Jang gave back,

465
00:43:51,830 --> 00:43:53,830
Take out all the money you've hidden away all these years.

466
00:43:53,830 --> 00:43:55,110
There is no such thing, little bitch!

467
00:43:55,110 --> 00:43:56,230
- There isn't?
- No.

468
00:43:56,270 --> 00:43:57,480
- There really isn't?
- I said there isn't!

469
00:43:57,480 --> 00:43:59,240
- You're lying!
- You really...

470
00:43:59,240 --> 00:44:01,500
There's no way you wouldn't have any money! Hyo Seon's dad

471
00:44:01,500 --> 00:44:05,150
never cared where and how you spent his money.

472
00:44:05,150 --> 00:44:08,130
There's no way you didn't put your hand in an open wallet.

473
00:44:08,130 --> 00:44:10,810
You think I don't know you, Mom? How much did you take?

474
00:44:10,810 --> 00:44:13,440
Take out all the money you've hidden!

475
00:44:13,440 --> 00:44:15,660
You've gone crazy, haven't you?

476
00:44:15,660 --> 00:44:20,050
Even if I did, what about you, me and Joon Soo's future?

477
00:44:20,050 --> 00:44:22,960
Do you think I'll dump money on a failing company just like that?

478
00:44:22,960 --> 00:44:25,900
I'll pay it back with interest!

479
00:44:25,900 --> 00:44:29,890
- You really must be my daughter, judging from your bluffs.
- Hand it over!

480
00:44:29,890 --> 00:44:32,370
It's dirty money I exchanged for my dirty fortune.

481
00:44:32,370 --> 00:44:34,900
What right do you have to tell me give you that money?

482
00:44:34,900 --> 00:44:37,770
- I won't give it to you! I can't give it to you!
- Mom!

483
00:44:37,770 --> 00:44:39,080
- Let go of me.
- Mom!

484
00:44:39,080 --> 00:44:41,680
- I said let go of me.
- Mom, please give it to me!

485
00:44:41,680 --> 00:44:44,600
Hey. Get away from me, you bitch!

486
00:44:44,600 --> 00:44:48,020
Don't open your mouth in front of me. Don't say a single word.

487
00:44:48,020 --> 00:44:52,900
Don't touch me. Just try to speak a word to me.

488
00:45:41,940 --> 00:45:44,170
Is that how it was?

489
00:45:47,500 --> 00:45:49,390
Mom...

490
00:45:51,750 --> 00:45:53,910
Is that what Mom was doing?

491
00:45:57,140 --> 00:45:59,460
It's a lie, right?

492
00:46:01,860 --> 00:46:06,190
I must not have heard correctly, right?

493
00:46:16,990 --> 00:46:20,260
Are you just looking at me like that because my words don't seem like words to you?

494
00:46:20,260 --> 00:46:23,010
I told you to pack your things! What are you still doing?

495
00:46:23,010 --> 00:46:26,200
But, why are you... suddenly?

496
00:46:26,200 --> 00:46:29,680
Madam, if there's something we did wrong, please tell us.

497
00:46:29,680 --> 00:46:33,930
I don't want to listen to you, so leave.

498
00:46:33,930 --> 00:46:38,380
Call me once you've packed your things. I'll pay you up to today's workday.

499
00:46:38,380 --> 00:46:40,640
Madam...

500
00:46:40,640 --> 00:46:43,070
What are we going to do?!

501
00:47:00,570 --> 00:47:02,560
Grandmother!

502
00:47:03,620 --> 00:47:05,320
Grandmother!

503
00:47:05,320 --> 00:47:07,740
Ahjumma! Where are you going?

504
00:47:07,740 --> 00:47:10,250
Where are you going?

505
